model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      constraint "Production admits a release only when a fresh primary HTTP connection gauge plus the configured seven-client envelope fits max_connections minus configured reserved slots and the observed ceiling matches the approved configuration. The filtered database-only apply consumes budget.hash before migrations and the migration hash before pool provisioning. Those commands are keyed on what they read, so the full application apply finds them unchanged, and a database failure cannot apply runtime adapters, shells, container rollouts or publication receipts. Committed database changes survive later application failures and must remain compatible with the preceding runtime adapters."
    }
  }
}
